# The static-website pack's five keys — every repo-specific value the vendored
# release pipeline reads. Explicit on purpose: nothing is published, versioned,
# built or tested here except what this file names.
#
# The published site is site/ — index.html and the two files it loads, plus the
# privacy page it links. The research trees, the agent tooling and this config
# itself are not part of the site and so are not listed.
publish_root=site
publish_paths=index.html privacy.html styles.css analytics.js

version_files=package.json

# The Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token is public (it ships to every
# visitor) and lives in the CLOUDFLARE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN repo variable, which the
# pipeline exports into this command's environment. Unset — a fork, a repo that
# never configured it — substitutes the empty string, and analytics.js treats an
# empty token as "stay off", which is the safe outcome.
build_command=sed -i "s#REPLACE_WITH_CLOUDFLARE_WEB_ANALYTICS_TOKEN#${CLOUDFLARE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN}#" site/analytics.js

# The site is hand-authored and has no test suite of its own yet; the PR gate
# still runs the Claudinite world sweep and the artifact-assembly dry run.
test_command=
